captured
docket 0.2.0b3 (scratch install, rack-cli develop c982046f, contains P35-5 75b7e3fc)

Real `docket harness run --contract 1.1 --answers stdin --workspace <dir> --task-file <file>
--model gw/local/qwen3-35b --agent-id capture-ask-1 --timeout 60` transcript, against a
throwaway loopback HTTP server standing in for the model endpoint (DOCKET_HOME in a scratch
directory, DOCKET_LLM_API_KEY an obviously fake key). The server answered one `bash` tool call
(`git push origin production`, which docket's own `prod-deploy` action class gates), then a final
message. docket paused on the call and printed `approval_requested`; the one answer line
`{"v":"1.1.0","token":<the run's token>,"answer":{"approvalToken":<payload.token>,"action":
"accept","content":null}}` was written to its stdin, and the run finished `ok` with the approval
listed as `accepted`. A second run answering `decline` finished `ok` with `declined` and a
`tool_result` of `decision: deny, executed: false`. The approval's own token is `payload.token`
(the answer line names it `approvalToken`); `payload.options` offers approve_once, approve_task
and deny. The scratch directory is rewritten to `/capture` and nothing else changed.
